WEBVTT

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.920
[man]

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.920
Boy! The tide is on the turn!

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.400
I'm not warning you again!

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.520
[boy] Ships! There!

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:36.320
Danes... The devil's turds.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.600
Are they traders?

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.640
No. They come as Vikings.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.640
We go!

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.240
Go! Go!

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.080
[all grunting]

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:34.680
Where's my son?

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:38.120
Uhtred, take a half-dozen men

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:38.120
and ride to the river.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.200
There are Pagans there, you watch

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.200
them, see how many they are!

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.080
-Of course, Father.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.080
-Do nothing more. You understand?

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.480
-Yes, Father.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.480
-Oswart, what is it?

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.200
Ships!

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.200
I saw them first from the beach.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.280
-What ships?

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.280
-Danes.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:50.400
They're heading for the river!

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:51.880
[gasps]

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.640
Oh, God and his saints

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.640
preserve us, they have no soul.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.800
-We must pray.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.800
-We must act.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.760
Uhtred, do not fight them,

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.760
not a single one.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.720
-Be back by night fall.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.720
-Yes, Father.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.320
They are sent by God

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.320
to punish us for our sins.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.040
Our sins be damned, they are here to

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.040
support the Viking army in Eoferwic.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.200
You must instruct the priest

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.200
to pray for our deliverance.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.280
-Alferic!

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.280
-Lord?

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.600
Get them inside!

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.640
We take in as many

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.640
women and elders as we can,

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.760
and the rest to higher

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.760
ground and out of sight.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.000
Send word to rouse the country.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.760
I want every man

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.760
inside this fortress.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.600
And every man

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.600
must be prepared to die.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:21.520
[wind whistling]

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.280
-[man] Port side ready to row!

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.280
-[man 2] Port side ready to row!

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.760
-Starboard side ready to row!

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.760
-Starboard side ready to row!

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.840
[men grunting]

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.160
Father.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:43.040
-[men grunting]

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:43.040
-[man orders, indistinct]

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.200
Taste.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.200
[indistinct]

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.960
-Fresh.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.960
-Sweet water.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.800
-Yes.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.800
-What else do you see?

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:01.840
[exhales] I see a clear river,

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:01.840
fish as big as a man's leg.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.440
I see a forest alive with meat,

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:06.960
and more than that, I see

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:06.960
a place to grow fat and old.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.680
[horses whinny]

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.280
Horses.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:15.760
Yeah, and I see spies,

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:15.760
shitting themselves.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.960
[men] Yeah!

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:21.560
[men yelling indistinct]

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:28.840
We'll meet sword with sword!

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:28.840
You are pagans!

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.440
We have the greater god

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.440
on our side!

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.120
Kjartan, I think we should

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.120
teach that boy a lesson.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:38.960
-Taking her in. At speed.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:38.960
-[man] Take her to speed!

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.280
[men grunting]

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.640
[baby crying]

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.840
[man yells indistinct]

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:01.240
Why do I leave the villages

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:01.240
unprotected, and bring the men inside?

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.040
Is that your question?

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:07.120
A village can be rebuilt,

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:07.120
a warrior can die only once.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.000
The Danes maybe

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.000
heading south to Eoferwic.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.120
But they will kill

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.120
whoever they can on the way.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.080
Now go find the priest.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:17.840
Yes, Father.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:28.720
[man] Come in, Osbert,

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:28.720
don't skulk in the shadows.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.240
He, uh, wants to know

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.240
if you're ready?

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:35.200
Almost. Do you know

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:35.200
what I am tasked with?

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:37.320
Um, a letter?

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.640
A response to a letter,

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.640
this letter, from King Aella,

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:45.040
asking your father

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:45.040
for his support; his army,

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.080
to help recapture

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.080
the City of Eoferwic.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.840
This is why it is important for

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.840
you to be able to read and write.

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:52.280
Father can't read nor write.

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:54.640
Yeah, well, for your father

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:54.640
it's too late.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:57.400
King Aella could have

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:57.400
sent a man on horseback.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:00.080
Yeah, but who's to say the man

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:00.080
on horseback speaks the truth?

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:03.240
Or has remembered

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:03.240
the true message?

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:07.080
What these letters will

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:07.080
represent is history; facts...

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:10.440
Your father is informing

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:10.440
King Aella, and King Osbert,

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:13.640
he will be alongside

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:13.640
their armies at Eoferwic.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.880
And the mark of Bebbanburg

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.880
will guarantee the truth of it.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.640
Why do we fight for Eoferwic?

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:23.480
Well, we fight for Eoferwic because

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:23.480
we do not wish to see England,

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.960
piece-by-piece,

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.960
become Daneland.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:27.280
[chuckles]

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:29.840
I heard it said that we

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:29.840
were Pagans once;

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:32.560
that Woden and Odin

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:32.560
are the same.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:35.040
We saw the error of our ways

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:35.040
and we looked to Rome.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.880
I heard the Pagans

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.880
have fierce Gods of War.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.080
Well, we are right

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.080
and they are mistaken.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.120
Osbert, we are blessed.

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:44.880
I should make you swear

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:44.880
on St. Cuthbert's comb

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.800
never to mention

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.800
the likes of Woden again.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.960
But what if I had

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.960
a hound called Woden?

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:51.680
What if I didn't,

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:51.680
what would you do then?

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:52.880
-You haven't, you have not!

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:52.880
-What would you do then?

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:53.960
What if you had

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:53.960
a pig called, Thor?

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.560
Come; let's go

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.560
see your father? Come!

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:56.600
A pig called, Thor...

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.920
Is it really

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.920
St. Cuthbert's comb?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.720
Of course,

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.720
it's St. Cuthbert's comb,

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:03.480
and his holy hair

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:03.480
lies in the teeth of the comb.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.760
Where was your father last?

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:07.280
He was humping the servant girl.

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.440
-That's a lie, Osbert.

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.440
-No.

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:11.560
Are you never

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:11.560
gonna tire of teasing?

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:12.600
Nope!

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:15.480
[man] Horsemen approaching!

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:35.240
He rides Uhtred's horse.

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:43.160
Osbert?!

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:03.280
No!

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:03.280
[yells]

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:18.640
Bury what's left of him.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:25.080
[panting]

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:29.720
Osbert. Come on...

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.640
Remind me of the last words

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.640
I spoke to him.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.800
You told him to watch,

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.800
do not fight.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:37.320
We have no idea

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:37.320
of the circumstance--

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:39.080
-Do not fight, means do not fight.

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:39.080
-He was young.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:41.400
There was no fight

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:41.400
to be had until Eoferwic.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:44.000
You wanted to see Osbert,

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:44.000
my Lord.

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:46.080
You...

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:48.680
You are now called Uhtred.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:48.680
Uhtred, son of Uhtred.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:51.440
-You have your stone, the amber?

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:51.440
-Yes, Father.

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:53.640
The priest will show you

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:53.640
your history, the parchments.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:55.120
Make him understand who he is.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.800
[priest] Lord, I... I should

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.800
like to baptize him again.

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:00.280
Well, if he arrives

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:00.280
at Heavens gate as Uhtred,

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:02.160
they may wonder

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:02.160
what's happened to Osbert.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:05.280
Do what you must,

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:05.280
but do as I ask.

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:07.200
Lord.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.960
We were kings here once, boy!

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:13.520
Kings of all the lands between

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:13.520
the Rivers Tuede and Tine.

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:15.040
And we should be kings again.

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:16.480
Yes, we should,

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:16.480
but it doesn't matter

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:18.920
what they call us,

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:18.920
so long as they obey.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:24.120
Our ancestors took this land, and it has

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:24.120
been strengthened with our blood and bone.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:28.240
And now you are the new heir

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:28.240
of Bebbanburg, do you hear me?

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:30.120
And you will

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:30.120
die for it if needed.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.040
Yes, Father.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.040
And I will give you the head

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.280
of the man

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.280
who killed Uhtred.

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:35.400
No, you are Uhtred!

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:37.320
Have you not been

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:37.320
listening to me!

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:40.640
Do not tell me what it is you

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:40.640
will do, you are just a pup!

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:45.640
You will give me nothing, you

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:45.640
will watch and you will learn!

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:50.680
Put him in the water before his

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:50.680
mother's tongue gives me grief.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:52.160
She's not my mother.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:58.080
Will you take him with you to battle

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:58.080
to watch and learn? He's old enough.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.120
I need you to choose 30 men

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.120
and remain here at Bebbanburg.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.560
Protect the boy,

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.560
he is the heir.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:07.120
Thirty will hold

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:07.120
and is few enough to feed.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:08.160
Will you do this for me?

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:09.400
I'd rather

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:09.400
be with you at Eoferwic,

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:11.920
-but I'll do as you ask.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:11.920
-Thank you.

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:15.240
[indistinct chatter]

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:18.200
Come on, quickly.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:18.200
Up there, go on.

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:21.640
[man] Hurry, please.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:25.920
[shivering]

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:37.600
Heavenly Father,

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:37.600
receive your servant, Uhtred,

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:40.360
into the Holy kind of the Saints

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:45.120
and into the ranks

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:45.120
of the most bright angels.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:50.920
Let your holy waters cleanse him and

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:50.920
make him worthy of your blessing.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:55.680
Make him your instrument

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:55.680
and your rod.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:01.800
Let him realize the significance

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:01.800
of the written word

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:04.160
so that he may

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:04.160
learn of your glory

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:07.480
and in turn,

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:07.480
may spread your word.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:09.000
[water bubbling]

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:11.920
-Beo--

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:11.920
-Let him grow in wisdom

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:17.000
and in respect, so he may

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:17.000
lead in a Godly manner.

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:18.320
Beocca he's cleansed.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:20.160
Amen.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:21.240
[gasps]

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.920
Uhtred, son of

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.920
Uhtred of Bebbanburg,

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.200
welcome to

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.200
the Christian world.

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:29.400
Behold your people

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:29.400
and your lands.

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:31.920
[cheering]

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:01.360
[birds squawking]

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:03.960
[footsteps approaching]

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:13.840
Where are the people,

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:13.840
the soldiers?

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.640
On the road to Eoferwic;

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.640
led by your father.

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:18.120
He will join the two other

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:18.120
kings of Northumbria.

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:19.680
With... Without me?

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.480
You are to remain at Bebbanburg

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.480
with your kindly uncle.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:23.920
I am sworn to keep you safe.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.520
Should you wish to fight

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.520
we can always arm-wrestle.

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:28.000
-Where's the priest?

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:28.000
-With your father. Eat.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.240
You have work to do,

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.240
Uhtred, in the stables;

00:12:31.320 --> 00:12:34.640
Thankfully,

00:12:31.320 --> 00:12:34.640
we have been left horses.

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:37.040
-You should eat.

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:37.040
-I'm not hungry.

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:39.800
We have work to do,

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:39.800
horse shit to shovel.

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:42.720
Come and find me

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:42.720
when you've finished.

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:53.960
[door shuts]

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:31.440
Scallion, if my brother falls

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:31.440
in battle, the boy must fall.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:40.280
[indistinct chatter]

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:50.800
[man coughing]

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:07.360
[dog barking]

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:13.400
All this way

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:13.400
and no reception party.

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:15.480
Earl Ragnar.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:17.760
Guthrum!

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:21.120
-How are you?

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:21.120
-I'm fine, I'm hungry!

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:22.560
-And your boy?

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:22.560
-He's coming.

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:24.880
-Ragnar.

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:24.880
-Ubba, I brought men and horses.

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:26.880
Good to see you, are you well?

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:29.680
[men laughing]

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:34.280
You made a gift of his own son's

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:34.280
head? How did this Lord react?

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:35.840
He did nothing.

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:40.200
He brought his warriors into the

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:40.200
fortress and kept them inside.

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:41.760
It was not cowardice.

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:45.200
Restraint.

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:45.200
He is saving his men.

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:47.080
That man is Uhtred.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:49.560
One of the three kings

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:49.560
of Northumbria, a warrior king.

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:52.960
The other two are fools, they would

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:52.960
rather be here fighting each other.

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:54.680
This is true?

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:57.440
King Aella

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:57.440
and King Osbert, they, uh,

00:14:57.520 --> 00:15:00.360
both lay claim to Eoferwic.

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:02.720
They have

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:02.720
the strangest of names.

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:05.280
-[chuckles]

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:05.280
-So, when do we fight?

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:06.960
Soon, I hope.

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:10.560
I am still to decide.

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:18.640
Fools or not,

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:18.640
they have three armies.

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:22.760
-They have numbers.

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:22.760
-[Ragnar] But are divided.

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:26.840
Three kings, but only one who

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:26.840
can lead them, this Uhtred...

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:30.520
Then we kill him and Northumbria

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:30.520
is ours, all of it.

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:32.920
[laughing]

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:36.160
Listen to him, listen to the

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:36.160
boy, he reminds me of me!

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:38.560
Yeah, when you were younger.

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:41.200
Of course, when I was younger.

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:41.200
He's just a boy.

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:44.240
-Just saying.

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:44.240
-Ubba, did you say I was old?

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:46.720
-Storri? I'm not getting old.

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:46.720
-No.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:50.960
Ubba, I have seen

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:50.960
the land outside the city.

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:53.520
I have a plan in mind,

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:53.520
a good plan.

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:57.520
And my son would like

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:57.520
to wet his sword, with you.

00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:59.480
So do we fight?

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.000
Storri?

00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:06.880
The signs are good.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:08.240
Only this morning I saw a raven,

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.360
flying towards the Saxon camp,

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.600
and he was asking me to follow,

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.600
I'm sure of it.

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:15.800
Hmm...

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:15.800
[whispering indistinct]

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:20.760
Then we fight.

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:23.520
[men cheering]

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:49.240
[Osbert]

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:49.240
What kind of hell is this?

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:52.520
It's a Pagan's hell.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:52.520
We out number them!

00:16:52.600 --> 00:16:55.160
But there are more,

00:16:52.600 --> 00:16:55.160
there must be...

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:58.080
Nothing changes,

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:58.080
we attack with half our number,

00:16:58.160 --> 00:16:59.480
the second half have to follow,

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:00.680
once we have

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:00.680
the measure of them.

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:02.440
They have conceded

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:02.440
to higher ground.

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:05.360
Kingaler,

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:05.360
yours and Lord Uhtred's armies

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:06.920
will attack in the first wave.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:10.280
Prepare! Prepare!

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:11.680
[horns blow]

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:13.280
Shield!

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:16.600
No... No, not without me!

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:43.040
Come night fall,

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:43.040
we'll be rid of this plague

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:45.440
and counting our share

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:45.440
of the plunder!

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:47.840
[all yelling]

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:53.120
My shield!

00:17:56.240 --> 00:18:00.560
[all whispering indistinct]

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:23.320
[whispering stops]

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:05.080
Kill them all!

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:07.520
[all yelling]

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:18.640
[grunting]

00:19:25.520 --> 00:19:27.840
[Aella] The wall is holding.

00:19:27.920 --> 00:19:30.960
Go! Transfer all

00:19:27.920 --> 00:19:30.960
your shield and drive!

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:33.120
Drive!

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:35.200
Ease.

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:37.720
Ease!

00:19:39.560 --> 00:19:41.480
Ease!

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:43.840
Ease!

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:47.720
Push! Keep pushing!

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:47.720
It's working!

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.440
Drive them!

00:19:57.520 --> 00:19:59.880
[screaming]

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:05.520
[Beocca] They are tiring,

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:05.520
they can't fight back.

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:08.520
-We're winning, look.

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:08.520
-[man] We're winning...

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:11.600
[yells indistinct]

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:16.720
[yells indistinct]

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:22.360
Not yet! Not yet!

00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:39.480
Dear God, no...

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:43.120
[all yelling]

00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:48.360
Shield! Wall!

00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:49.760
[chanting]

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:52.840
Dear God, of infinite mercy,

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:52.840
not this!

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:59.520
Kill them all!

00:21:00.600 --> 00:21:02.400
[screams]

00:21:09.880 --> 00:21:13.880
Legs! Legs!

00:21:09.880 --> 00:21:13.880
Legs protect your legs!

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:16.680
Lift up your sword

00:21:16.760 --> 00:21:21.400
and spare these men of England

00:21:16.760 --> 00:21:21.400
who fight in your name.

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:24.520
Let the heathens hearts

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:24.520
crumble and wither.

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:28.320
Bestow your power

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:28.320
upon these men of England,

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:32.040
so they can glorify your name

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:32.040
with the blood of the devils.

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:35.440
Have mercy now lord,

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:39.920
do not forsake us,

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:39.920
do not forsake England.

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:51.760
Follow me! Follow me!

00:21:52.600 --> 00:21:53.800
Take him!

00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:56.520
[grunting]

00:21:58.800 --> 00:22:03.080
[Ragnar] Close the sealed wall!

00:21:58.800 --> 00:22:03.080
Close the wall and take him!

00:22:03.160 --> 00:22:05.600
[gasps]

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:08.800
No!

00:22:18.120 --> 00:22:20.360
[yelling]

00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:26.000
He's like a wasp.

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:37.160
-The wasp has lost its sting.

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:37.160
-Yeah.

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:38.600
[yelling]

00:22:38.680 --> 00:22:40.080
[groans]

00:22:40.160 --> 00:22:43.640
[panting]

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:45.960
[groans]

00:22:46.040 --> 00:22:49.440
Are you sure he's a Saxon?

00:22:46.040 --> 00:22:49.440
He fights like a Dane.

00:22:49.520 --> 00:22:51.360
Yeah.

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:54.160
[grunting]

00:22:57.760 --> 00:23:00.280
[indistinct chatter]

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:03.440
[dog barking]

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:03.440
[woman screaming]

00:23:10.600 --> 00:23:13.080
[screaming]

00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:38.320
Leave her!

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:41.520
She is to live!

00:23:42.520 --> 00:23:46.000
Some of these young ones

00:23:42.520 --> 00:23:46.000
can come in useful.

00:23:47.760 --> 00:23:51.000
Father,

00:23:47.760 --> 00:23:51.000
there's the boy I spoke of.

00:23:51.080 --> 00:23:55.440
The one who almost killed you?

00:23:51.080 --> 00:23:55.440
And you're leaving him with me?

00:23:55.520 --> 00:23:58.400
I've never seen a man

00:23:55.520 --> 00:23:58.400
get the better of you yet.

00:23:59.240 --> 00:24:02.480
[all cheering]

00:24:02.560 --> 00:24:05.480
[woman screaming]

00:24:14.080 --> 00:24:17.080
Cut me some chicken.

00:24:23.680 --> 00:24:28.840
Careful, the blade is sharp.

00:24:23.680 --> 00:24:28.840
It can kill a man.

00:24:35.480 --> 00:24:38.120
The chicken is on your platter.

00:24:44.360 --> 00:24:47.480
Have you always been blind?

00:24:47.560 --> 00:24:49.960
Oh, I see enough.

00:24:50.040 --> 00:24:54.320
So... who have

00:24:50.040 --> 00:24:54.320
they been killing below?

00:24:54.400 --> 00:24:55.760
[woman screaming]

00:24:55.840 --> 00:24:57.920
Prisoners...

00:25:00.600 --> 00:25:02.480
Just now a king.

00:25:02.560 --> 00:25:06.400
-Did he die well?

00:25:02.560 --> 00:25:06.400
-No.

00:25:06.480 --> 00:25:09.240
Then he shouldn't

00:25:06.480 --> 00:25:09.240
have been king.

00:25:11.920 --> 00:25:15.920
Tell me, who sits

00:25:11.920 --> 00:25:15.920
in the middle of the hall?

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:18.080
[yells]

00:25:21.200 --> 00:25:23.800
Is it a big man

00:25:21.200 --> 00:25:23.800
and a small man?

00:25:25.880 --> 00:25:28.800
Yes, and a gray man

00:25:25.880 --> 00:25:28.800
sits in between them.

00:25:28.880 --> 00:25:33.120
If you get to live, you should

00:25:28.880 --> 00:25:33.120
beware of the big man: Ubba.

00:25:33.200 --> 00:25:35.560
My advice for you is

00:25:35.640 --> 00:25:41.040
to never cross Ubba

00:25:35.640 --> 00:25:41.040
and never, never fight him.

00:25:41.120 --> 00:25:42.480
If I get to live?

00:25:42.560 --> 00:25:45.240
He listens to no one

00:25:42.560 --> 00:25:45.240
but the Gods.

00:25:45.320 --> 00:25:51.720
Men who take their orders from

00:25:45.320 --> 00:25:51.720
the Gods are unpredictable.

00:25:54.200 --> 00:25:57.720
What did you mean?

00:25:54.200 --> 00:25:57.720
When you said if I get to live?

00:25:57.800 --> 00:25:59.720
You're my prisoner.

00:26:01.160 --> 00:26:06.000
The gray man will be Egbert,

00:26:01.160 --> 00:26:06.000
he's a Saxon Aelderman.

00:26:06.080 --> 00:26:11.280
He has pledged allegiance

00:26:06.080 --> 00:26:11.280
and now he calls himself a king.

00:26:11.360 --> 00:26:14.040
He is king of nothing.

00:26:14.120 --> 00:26:18.960
Soon all of the kings in England

00:26:14.120 --> 00:26:18.960
shall be kings of nothing.

00:26:19.040 --> 00:26:23.760
Northumbria's ours,

00:26:19.040 --> 00:26:23.760
Mercia will soon by ours.

00:26:23.840 --> 00:26:26.600
Then East Anglia, Cornwallum

00:26:26.680 --> 00:26:32.600
and then the greatest prize

00:26:26.680 --> 00:26:32.600
is the last kingdom: Wessex.

00:26:32.680 --> 00:26:34.480
I've heard of Wessex.

00:26:34.560 --> 00:26:37.240
Anything will grow in Wessex.

00:26:37.320 --> 00:26:39.360
[men groan]

00:26:39.440 --> 00:26:41.560
Tell me your name.

00:26:41.640 --> 00:26:45.920
Uhtred... I am

00:26:41.640 --> 00:26:45.920
the Aelderman of Bebbanburg.

00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:47.280
You are?

00:26:47.360 --> 00:26:49.080
I am...

00:26:47.360 --> 00:26:49.080
I own lands to the north.

00:26:49.160 --> 00:26:52.440
How long have you been

00:26:49.160 --> 00:26:52.440
the Aelderman of these lands?

00:26:58.440 --> 00:27:02.680
Your father chose to fight us.

00:27:02.760 --> 00:27:06.280
And is now... dead.

00:27:08.280 --> 00:27:12.640
He...

00:27:08.280 --> 00:27:12.640
He was not fond of me.

00:27:17.960 --> 00:27:23.360
I now understand why

00:27:17.960 --> 00:27:23.360
my son spared you...

00:27:23.440 --> 00:27:28.840
...Uhtred of Bebbanburg,

00:27:23.440 --> 00:27:28.840
you are a warrior.

00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:33.520
Have some ale.

00:27:35.960 --> 00:27:37.920
Drink it...

00:27:40.200 --> 00:27:42.320
...lots of it.

00:28:18.240 --> 00:28:19.840
Here.

00:28:21.400 --> 00:28:22.320
Take it up there.

00:28:22.400 --> 00:28:25.160
[clanging]

00:28:29.720 --> 00:28:32.200
I am thinking

00:28:29.720 --> 00:28:32.200
of keeping them both,

00:28:32.840 --> 00:28:36.360
the boy and the girl;

00:28:32.840 --> 00:28:36.360
they can help your mother.

00:28:37.960 --> 00:28:39.520
Disagree?

00:28:39.600 --> 00:28:43.840
No, but we did

00:28:39.600 --> 00:28:43.840
kill his father.

00:28:43.920 --> 00:28:47.160
And if he is an Aelderman,

00:28:43.920 --> 00:28:47.160
we could sell him for a ransom.

00:28:47.240 --> 00:28:49.080
Perhaps.

00:29:07.680 --> 00:29:10.160
[gasps softly]

00:29:49.400 --> 00:29:52.840
[water sloshing]

00:29:52.920 --> 00:29:55.120
Brida, be careful

00:29:52.920 --> 00:29:55.120
not to spill the water,

00:29:55.200 --> 00:29:56.920
you'll turn the floor to mud.

00:29:57.000 --> 00:30:00.880
Uhtred,

00:29:57.000 --> 00:30:00.880
wood needs to be chopped.

00:30:00.960 --> 00:30:03.520
Brida, you can do the goats.

00:30:03.600 --> 00:30:06.320
Will there be time

00:30:03.600 --> 00:30:06.320
for Uhtred to play?

00:30:06.400 --> 00:30:08.560
Only when work is done.

00:30:11.120 --> 00:30:14.200
I don't like our daughter

00:30:11.120 --> 00:30:14.200
having to play with the slaves.

00:30:14.280 --> 00:30:17.240
-They're only children.

00:30:14.280 --> 00:30:17.240
-They have a place.

00:30:17.320 --> 00:30:19.280
Grumpy...

00:30:24.600 --> 00:30:26.440
[man] My horse.

00:30:26.520 --> 00:30:29.320
Hey, Ragnar Ragnarson!

00:30:29.400 --> 00:30:32.320
Hey, Uhtred of wherever.

00:30:32.400 --> 00:30:34.240
How about you teach me

00:30:32.400 --> 00:30:34.240
how to use a sword.

00:30:34.320 --> 00:30:36.320
We don't teach slaves

00:30:34.320 --> 00:30:36.320
how to fight.

00:30:36.400 --> 00:30:39.280
That tongue of yours

00:30:36.400 --> 00:30:39.280
will be your death boy.

00:30:39.360 --> 00:30:41.760
Now get back to work!

00:30:43.560 --> 00:30:46.200
What does the play involve?

00:30:46.280 --> 00:30:48.560
We built a hall in the Gorge.

00:30:48.640 --> 00:30:51.080
I'm a mistress,

00:30:48.640 --> 00:30:51.080
Uhtred is a warrior.

00:30:51.160 --> 00:30:54.880
-Not a servant?

00:30:51.160 --> 00:30:54.880
-It is a game.

00:30:55.480 --> 00:30:58.280
[giggling]

00:30:58.360 --> 00:30:59.920
-[Uhtred] A wolf?

00:30:58.360 --> 00:30:59.920
-[Brida] Uhtred!

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:03.240
-That was it, a wolf.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:03.240
-Boar watch out!

00:31:03.320 --> 00:31:05.840
I saw it, it's sharp teeth

00:31:03.320 --> 00:31:05.840
and yellow eyes.

00:31:05.920 --> 00:31:07.880
Don't let the wolves

00:31:05.920 --> 00:31:07.880
get to me Uhtred.

00:31:07.960 --> 00:31:09.640
Use the fire to keep them away.

00:31:09.720 --> 00:31:12.960
I see them. They are as big

00:31:09.720 --> 00:31:12.960
as Ubba and smell worse.

00:31:13.040 --> 00:31:15.200
[chuckles]

00:31:16.800 --> 00:31:19.280
Did you see that?

00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:22.600
[twig snaps]

00:31:23.360 --> 00:31:24.840
[girl] Uhtred?

00:31:24.920 --> 00:31:26.880
Stay up there.

00:31:26.960 --> 00:31:29.440
[gasps] Look!

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:31.080
Uhtred, what is happening?

00:31:31.160 --> 00:31:32.720
Stay up there, Thyra.

00:31:32.800 --> 00:31:34.560
It's Sven, he won't hurt you.

00:31:34.640 --> 00:31:35.520
[Brida] But he'll kill us.

00:31:35.600 --> 00:31:37.360
[yelling]

00:31:37.440 --> 00:31:39.800
He will kill us! Run!

00:31:46.680 --> 00:31:48.720
That was a real sword!

00:31:48.800 --> 00:31:50.440
I saw it.

00:31:50.520 --> 00:31:51.640
[Thyra screams]

00:31:51.720 --> 00:31:54.560
-Uhtred! Uhtred!

00:31:51.720 --> 00:31:54.560
-Thyra.

00:32:04.640 --> 00:32:06.680
[gasps]

00:32:10.560 --> 00:32:12.840
[yelling]

00:32:16.960 --> 00:32:20.960
What's this?

00:32:16.960 --> 00:32:20.960
You been fighting again?

00:32:21.240 --> 00:32:23.040
Yes.

00:32:23.120 --> 00:32:24.440
With Sven?

00:32:24.520 --> 00:32:26.400
Kjartan's son?

00:32:26.680 --> 00:32:27.920
Yes.

00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:29.640
Uhtred,

00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:29.640
he's much bigger than you.

00:32:29.720 --> 00:32:31.840
-He's a turd.

00:32:29.720 --> 00:32:31.840
-Why do you say that?

00:32:31.920 --> 00:32:33.560
[man]

00:32:31.920 --> 00:32:33.560
Who started it?

00:32:34.560 --> 00:32:37.680
-Who began the fight?

00:32:34.560 --> 00:32:37.680
-I began the fight.

00:32:37.760 --> 00:32:40.600
For no other reason

00:32:37.760 --> 00:32:40.600
than that he's a turd?

00:32:40.680 --> 00:32:42.840
Danes have murdered for less.

00:32:42.920 --> 00:32:45.440
[woman]

00:32:42.920 --> 00:32:45.440
Uhtred, that's enough!

00:32:45.520 --> 00:32:47.920
-You want to be sold boy?

00:32:45.520 --> 00:32:47.920
-I wish to eat.

00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:50.200
-[man] Speak up.

00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:50.200
-I wish to eat!

00:32:50.280 --> 00:32:52.200
You want to eat?

00:32:54.360 --> 00:32:56.280
You want to eat?

00:32:56.360 --> 00:33:00.240
You know what?

00:32:56.360 --> 00:33:00.240
I say you starve.

00:33:00.320 --> 00:33:02.920
Fighting is expected,

00:33:00.320 --> 00:33:02.920
disobedience is not.

00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:04.040
[slapping]

00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:04.040
[grunts]

00:33:04.120 --> 00:33:06.160
Sven began the fight!

00:33:07.240 --> 00:33:11.280
Kjartan! Kjartan!

00:33:17.120 --> 00:33:19.760
Earl Ragnar, let me first say,

00:33:17.120 --> 00:33:19.760
he's a... he's a good boy.

00:33:19.840 --> 00:33:23.360
He brought this sword on to my

00:33:19.840 --> 00:33:23.360
land. I will have words with him.

00:33:23.440 --> 00:33:25.560
In time, he'll serve

00:33:23.440 --> 00:33:25.560
on your ship. He... he...

00:33:25.640 --> 00:33:26.920
He has offended me.

00:33:27.000 --> 00:33:28.240
He will honor you

00:33:27.000 --> 00:33:28.240
and he meant no harm, Lord.

00:33:28.320 --> 00:33:29.480
He meant no harm?

00:33:29.560 --> 00:33:31.640
He looked

00:33:29.560 --> 00:33:31.640
at my daughter's nakedness.

00:33:31.720 --> 00:33:34.320
And he was punished.

00:33:31.720 --> 00:33:34.320
Your Saxon slave cut him.

00:33:34.400 --> 00:33:36.360
Shall I make

00:33:34.400 --> 00:33:36.360
a square of branches?

00:33:36.440 --> 00:33:40.200
Are you gonna fight me

00:33:36.440 --> 00:33:40.200
for your son or fetch him?

00:33:44.760 --> 00:33:48.040
Sven! Come out here.

00:33:50.720 --> 00:33:52.200
Tell him what you have to say.

00:33:52.280 --> 00:33:54.120
-I'm sorry.

00:33:52.280 --> 00:33:54.120
-He can't hear you.

00:33:54.200 --> 00:33:56.640
I'm sorry, Lord,

00:33:54.200 --> 00:33:56.640
for what I did.

00:34:00.600 --> 00:34:05.600
You laid hands on my daughter.

00:34:00.600 --> 00:34:05.600
You stripped her naked.

00:34:05.680 --> 00:34:08.560
-Half-naked, Lord.

00:34:05.680 --> 00:34:08.560
-He is at an age, Lord.

00:34:10.240 --> 00:34:14.960
-Is this true, half-naked?

00:34:10.240 --> 00:34:14.960
-Yes, Lord.

00:34:16.720 --> 00:34:19.000
[exhales]

00:34:19.080 --> 00:34:22.160
Then I shall only

00:34:19.080 --> 00:34:22.160
take his one eye.

00:34:22.240 --> 00:34:23.680
[Kjartan]

00:34:22.240 --> 00:34:23.680
No, Lord, please!

00:34:23.760 --> 00:34:24.960
[grunting]

00:34:25.040 --> 00:34:28.480
Kjartan, you are

00:34:25.040 --> 00:34:28.480
banished from my land.

00:34:28.560 --> 00:34:31.600
[groaning in pain]

00:34:45.640 --> 00:34:48.040
[fire cackling]

00:34:51.080 --> 00:34:53.480
I have something for you.

00:34:54.480 --> 00:34:56.040
What is it?

00:34:56.120 --> 00:34:58.600
An amulet; Thor's hammer.

00:34:58.680 --> 00:35:00.480
Ah, but, um...

00:35:00.560 --> 00:35:01.680
But what?

00:35:01.760 --> 00:35:03.800
You're Christian.

00:35:04.920 --> 00:35:06.840
Take it.

00:35:09.360 --> 00:35:11.680
-I can't.

00:35:09.360 --> 00:35:11.680
-Don't you want it?

00:35:11.760 --> 00:35:13.760
-I... I do want it!

00:35:11.760 --> 00:35:13.760
-Take it!

00:35:13.840 --> 00:35:15.200
-I'm trying.

00:35:13.840 --> 00:35:15.200
-Take it!

00:35:15.280 --> 00:35:16.840
-[grunts]

00:35:15.280 --> 00:35:16.840
-I don't think he wants it.

00:35:16.920 --> 00:35:21.080
-I... I do want it!

00:35:16.920 --> 00:35:21.080
-No, I don't think so.

00:35:24.160 --> 00:35:26.000
Thank you.

00:35:27.560 --> 00:35:31.040
Tell me about Denmark...

00:35:32.280 --> 00:35:35.280
...your home.

00:35:35.360 --> 00:35:37.800
What can I say about Denmark?

00:35:38.040 --> 00:35:39.520
It's wet.

00:35:39.600 --> 00:35:45.600
And harsh... and the ground

00:35:39.600 --> 00:35:45.600
is so flat and sandy

00:35:45.680 --> 00:35:47.200
you can't grow a fart.

00:35:47.280 --> 00:35:49.800
Which is why

00:35:47.280 --> 00:35:49.800
we are here in England.

00:35:50.680 --> 00:35:52.000
To grow.

00:35:52.080 --> 00:35:56.040
And why young Ragnar

00:35:52.080 --> 00:35:56.040
will soon be going for Ireland.

00:35:56.120 --> 00:35:57.760
You leave to fight?

00:35:57.840 --> 00:36:00.600
To make my wealth.

00:36:00.680 --> 00:36:05.280
If you want land or silver

00:36:00.680 --> 00:36:05.280
you have to take it.

00:36:08.400 --> 00:36:14.440
You made me...

00:36:08.400 --> 00:36:14.440
proud today... Uhtred...

00:36:15.600 --> 00:36:17.800
You made me proud.

00:36:46.400 --> 00:36:49.680
[birds squawking]

00:36:49.760 --> 00:36:53.640
[Alferic] I don't know you, you don't

00:36:49.760 --> 00:36:53.640
have the appearance of a messenger

00:36:53.720 --> 00:36:56.080
and Ubba's payments not yet due.

00:36:56.160 --> 00:36:59.440
No, Lord, I was a ship's master.

00:36:59.520 --> 00:37:03.680
Ah, well I have no ships,

00:36:59.520 --> 00:37:03.680
I need no ship's master.

00:37:07.400 --> 00:37:10.080
I have news

00:37:07.400 --> 00:37:10.080
that you will want to hear.

00:37:11.520 --> 00:37:12.680
Well...

00:37:12.760 --> 00:37:14.560
I would want something

00:37:12.760 --> 00:37:14.560
in return, Lord.

00:37:14.640 --> 00:37:15.520
[scoffs]

00:37:15.600 --> 00:37:17.480
Not now, not quite.

00:37:17.560 --> 00:37:21.360
But perhaps we could continue

00:37:17.560 --> 00:37:21.360
to help each other.

00:37:21.680 --> 00:37:23.040
Perhaps.

00:37:23.120 --> 00:37:25.280
Two days south of here.

00:37:25.360 --> 00:37:31.160
This little rat with the man I used

00:37:25.360 --> 00:37:31.160
to serve until he banished me.

00:37:31.720 --> 00:37:37.040
He has a slave, treats him well.

00:37:37.120 --> 00:37:42.160
This is a slave you are entitled

00:37:37.120 --> 00:37:42.160
to buy back if you wish to.

00:37:42.840 --> 00:37:44.040
Buy back?

00:37:44.120 --> 00:37:49.720
It's your nephew, Uhtred,

00:37:44.120 --> 00:37:49.720
Lord. He lives.

00:37:56.680 --> 00:37:59.440
[men talking indistinct]

00:38:04.520 --> 00:38:07.920
[Uhtred] What if I'm

00:38:04.520 --> 00:38:07.920
against being ransomed?

00:38:08.000 --> 00:38:12.400
Your family has discovered

00:38:08.000 --> 00:38:12.400
that you're still alive,

00:38:12.480 --> 00:38:17.760
and they wish for you to be

00:38:12.480 --> 00:38:17.760
returned; but they must pay.

00:38:17.840 --> 00:38:19.320
Pay Ragnar?

00:38:19.400 --> 00:38:24.080
Ubba takes more than half.

00:38:19.400 --> 00:38:24.080
It's normal.

00:38:28.040 --> 00:38:30.400
But I have no family.

00:38:33.520 --> 00:38:36.720
Keep them over there,

00:38:33.520 --> 00:38:36.720
tether the horses.

00:38:41.040 --> 00:38:43.080
Scallion, here.

00:38:45.400 --> 00:38:49.000
Uhtred.

00:38:45.400 --> 00:38:49.000
Are they treating you well?

00:38:49.080 --> 00:38:50.880
I am fed, yes.

00:38:50.960 --> 00:38:53.320
Good, good.

00:38:50.960 --> 00:38:53.320
That's all we ask.

00:38:54.520 --> 00:38:56.800
And what is this around

00:38:54.520 --> 00:38:56.800
your neck, some symbol?

00:38:56.880 --> 00:38:59.040
Oh, this...

00:38:56.880 --> 00:38:59.040
They make me wear it.

00:38:59.120 --> 00:39:00.760
May I see it?

00:39:07.080 --> 00:39:12.080
Look, I will speak plainly;

00:39:07.080 --> 00:39:12.080
your uncle will kill you.

00:39:12.160 --> 00:39:17.120
Right, you can not go back to

00:39:12.160 --> 00:39:17.120
Bebbanburg, you must escape.

00:39:17.200 --> 00:39:19.880
He wants to be the Aelderman;

00:39:17.200 --> 00:39:19.880
he wants to be a king, in fact,

00:39:19.960 --> 00:39:22.000
like the pathetic

00:39:19.960 --> 00:39:22.000
Egbert over there.

00:39:22.080 --> 00:39:24.800
A puppet king for his

00:39:22.080 --> 00:39:24.800
Danish masters.

00:39:24.880 --> 00:39:26.120
You should go to Wessex.

00:39:26.200 --> 00:39:27.400
King Aethelred,

00:39:26.200 --> 00:39:27.400
real King Aethelred

00:39:27.480 --> 00:39:28.800
and his brother,

00:39:27.480 --> 00:39:28.800
the Prince Alfred:

00:39:28.880 --> 00:39:31.000
they are good men,

00:39:28.880 --> 00:39:31.000
good Christian men.

00:39:31.080 --> 00:39:34.920
[Ragnar] That is enough

00:39:31.080 --> 00:39:34.920
whispering in his ear, priest.

00:39:35.000 --> 00:39:38.720
-Uhtred.

00:39:35.000 --> 00:39:38.720
-One more word and I'll have your ball-bag for a purse.

00:39:38.800 --> 00:39:40.120
[whispering]

00:39:38.800 --> 00:39:40.120
I will meet you there.

00:39:40.200 --> 00:39:42.800
[normal voice]

00:39:40.200 --> 00:39:42.800
That will not be necessary.

00:39:43.760 --> 00:39:45.320
What did he say?

00:39:45.400 --> 00:39:49.000
He... He asked if you were

00:39:45.400 --> 00:39:49.000
treating me well.

00:40:07.880 --> 00:40:09.880
-How much?

00:40:07.880 --> 00:40:09.880
-Three hundred.

00:40:09.960 --> 00:40:11.320
That is a ridiculous amount.

00:40:11.400 --> 00:40:13.560
How can a boy be worth

00:40:11.400 --> 00:40:13.560
300 pieces of silver?

00:40:13.640 --> 00:40:19.520
Because I say so, because

00:40:13.640 --> 00:40:19.520
he is a Lord, an Aelderman.

00:40:19.600 --> 00:40:20.920
He is a boy.

00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:22.920
I am the Aelderman

00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:22.920
of Bebbanburg.

00:40:23.000 --> 00:40:24.560
I carry the seal

00:40:23.000 --> 00:40:24.560
and the banner.

00:40:24.640 --> 00:40:27.440
That seal is my father's,

00:40:24.640 --> 00:40:27.440
which is now mine!

00:40:27.520 --> 00:40:30.640
You will be silent.

00:40:27.520 --> 00:40:30.640
You are for sale, nothing more.

00:40:30.720 --> 00:40:32.840
-For ransom, Lord.

00:40:30.720 --> 00:40:32.840
-That's is what I said.

00:40:32.920 --> 00:40:36.400
My Lords,

00:40:32.920 --> 00:40:36.400
I have given up land, horses;

00:40:36.480 --> 00:40:39.360
I have offered a generous supply

00:40:36.480 --> 00:40:39.360
of food as well as my sword.

00:40:39.440 --> 00:40:43.240
All I ask in return is a

00:40:39.440 --> 00:40:43.240
fair price for my only nephew.

00:40:43.320 --> 00:40:45.880
[man] What would you say

00:40:43.320 --> 00:40:45.880
is a fair price?

00:40:45.960 --> 00:40:47.720
[Alferic] I will offer

00:40:45.960 --> 00:40:47.720
100 pieces of silver.

00:40:47.800 --> 00:40:49.280
[man] Two hundred.

00:40:49.360 --> 00:40:53.480
My allegiance and 100 pieces

00:40:49.360 --> 00:40:53.480
is surely a fair price.

00:40:53.560 --> 00:40:57.080
[man] It is not.

00:40:57.160 --> 00:41:00.240
I will give 120 pieces

00:40:57.160 --> 00:41:00.240
of silver for the boy.

00:41:00.320 --> 00:41:03.480
[man chuckles]

00:41:00.320 --> 00:41:03.480
Not enough!

00:41:05.360 --> 00:41:09.440
Very well, 200 pieces.

00:41:09.520 --> 00:41:12.640
I agree to your terms.

00:41:14.640 --> 00:41:17.360
[whispering indistinct]

00:41:21.800 --> 00:41:23.560
The boy's sold to Earl Ragnar.

00:41:23.640 --> 00:41:25.880
-What?

00:41:23.640 --> 00:41:25.880
-Ransomed, Lord!

00:41:25.960 --> 00:41:28.880
That's what I said!

00:41:25.960 --> 00:41:28.880
So the matter is closed!

00:41:28.960 --> 00:41:31.040
My Lords,

00:41:28.960 --> 00:41:31.040
I have come a long way.

00:41:31.120 --> 00:41:32.360
I have offered my allegiance.

00:41:32.440 --> 00:41:35.360
Which is why you are

00:41:32.440 --> 00:41:35.360
allowed to breathe.

00:41:37.320 --> 00:41:40.600
If you have an

00:41:37.320 --> 00:41:40.600
argument it's with me now.

00:41:48.600 --> 00:41:52.160
If business is done,

00:41:48.600 --> 00:41:52.160
we have ale to drink.

00:41:52.240 --> 00:41:53.920
And King Egbert needs to sit.

00:41:54.000 --> 00:41:57.040
[laughing]

00:42:04.520 --> 00:42:06.400
[Uhtred]

00:42:04.520 --> 00:42:06.400
Am I not for ransom anymore?

00:42:06.480 --> 00:42:11.240
[Ragnar]

00:42:06.480 --> 00:42:11.240
You heard Ubba, I bought you.

00:42:11.320 --> 00:42:14.600
I thought I might

00:42:11.320 --> 00:42:14.600
sacrifice you to Odin.

00:42:15.240 --> 00:42:17.080
You bought me for how much?

00:42:17.160 --> 00:42:20.000
-Too much.

00:42:17.160 --> 00:42:20.000
-How much is too much?

00:42:20.080 --> 00:42:22.400
My swords weight in silver.

00:42:22.480 --> 00:42:24.640
I agree, I may have been robbed,

00:42:24.720 --> 00:42:29.440
but we like you boy,

00:42:24.720 --> 00:42:29.440
we're going to keep you.

00:42:29.520 --> 00:42:31.320
Does this mean I'm a Dane?

00:42:31.400 --> 00:42:35.720
It means is that you are Uhtred

00:42:31.400 --> 00:42:35.720
Ragnarson. You are a son to me now.

00:42:35.800 --> 00:42:37.560
[yelps]

00:43:05.240 --> 00:43:08.000
Brida, not that way!

00:43:05.240 --> 00:43:08.000
Take the goat out the side.

00:43:08.080 --> 00:43:09.840
Next time, I promise!

00:43:09.920 --> 00:43:11.080
Mother, look!

00:43:11.160 --> 00:43:13.200
It's beautiful, it really is.

00:43:13.280 --> 00:43:16.080
I can't believe

00:43:13.280 --> 00:43:16.080
I'm loosing you already!

00:43:16.160 --> 00:43:18.360
I will be

00:43:16.160 --> 00:43:18.360
living across the field.

00:43:18.440 --> 00:43:22.720
And if he does not treat you well, you just

00:43:18.440 --> 00:43:22.720
come marching right back across that field.

00:43:36.120 --> 00:43:39.760
Oh, look at this place...

00:43:39.840 --> 00:43:44.040
Uhtred, do you like

00:43:39.840 --> 00:43:44.040
my wedding necklace?

00:43:44.120 --> 00:43:46.840
I do, very pretty.

00:43:46.920 --> 00:43:50.200
He doesn't know

00:43:46.920 --> 00:43:50.200
anything about necklaces.

00:43:51.080 --> 00:43:52.880
You might as well ask me.

00:43:52.960 --> 00:43:55.760
Uhtred, with me; you can help me

00:43:52.960 --> 00:43:55.760
slaughter the goats.

00:43:55.840 --> 00:43:57.120
I've only just washed.

00:43:57.200 --> 00:44:00.680
[chuckles]

00:43:57.200 --> 00:44:00.680
The goats will be pleased.

00:44:04.840 --> 00:44:06.560
Later you can sweep the floor.

00:44:06.640 --> 00:44:09.600
[gasps]

00:44:06.640 --> 00:44:09.600
[laughing]

00:44:10.440 --> 00:44:12.160
Move over!

00:44:14.760 --> 00:44:17.840
This is an excuse to talk,

00:44:14.760 --> 00:44:17.840
that's all.

00:44:17.920 --> 00:44:21.920
With Thyra to be married; maybe it's

00:44:17.920 --> 00:44:21.920
time you got together with Brida.

00:44:22.000 --> 00:44:24.840
There are men, good men,

00:44:22.000 --> 00:44:24.840
asking about her.

00:44:24.920 --> 00:44:29.400
So you have to decide what you are

00:44:24.920 --> 00:44:29.400
to her, what you are to each other.

00:44:29.480 --> 00:44:31.000
[chuckling]

00:44:29.480 --> 00:44:31.000
Brida has her own mind.

00:44:31.080 --> 00:44:34.800
She has... but I see

00:44:31.080 --> 00:44:34.800
the way she looks at you.

00:44:34.880 --> 00:44:39.080
She's watching the charcoal

00:44:34.880 --> 00:44:39.080
tonight in the woods.

00:44:39.160 --> 00:44:42.000
Take my horse and join her.

00:44:42.080 --> 00:44:46.360
-The earth will be warm.

00:44:42.080 --> 00:44:46.360
-[laughing]

00:44:46.440 --> 00:44:49.800
Why not?

00:44:49.880 --> 00:44:54.000
I just thought in order to be a

00:44:49.880 --> 00:44:54.000
real Dane I had to marry a Dane.

00:44:55.160 --> 00:44:56.440
[sighs]

00:44:56.520 --> 00:44:58.000
Come on.

00:44:58.880 --> 00:45:02.120
I love you

00:44:58.880 --> 00:45:02.120
like I love young Ragnar.

00:45:16.160 --> 00:45:19.640
[indistinct chatter]

00:45:34.080 --> 00:45:36.000
What are you doing here?

00:46:05.560 --> 00:46:08.120
[breathing heavily]

00:46:12.040 --> 00:46:15.000
[moaning]

00:46:17.480 --> 00:46:20.440
[both giggling]

00:46:29.960 --> 00:46:33.000
Do you ever think of

00:46:29.960 --> 00:46:33.000
your English life?

00:46:36.000 --> 00:46:39.200
Who you were

00:46:36.000 --> 00:46:39.200
before we came to Ragnar?

00:46:41.120 --> 00:46:43.040
No.

00:46:44.720 --> 00:46:46.680
Do you?

00:46:50.680 --> 00:46:52.320
-I think of who I--

00:46:50.680 --> 00:46:52.320
-Shh!

00:46:52.400 --> 00:46:53.920
[men whispering]

00:46:55.720 --> 00:46:57.680
Voices...

00:46:59.040 --> 00:47:01.440
Men below.

00:47:16.840 --> 00:47:19.560
Danes. Who are they?

00:47:19.640 --> 00:47:21.160
[man whispers]

00:47:19.640 --> 00:47:21.160
This way...

00:47:21.240 --> 00:47:25.320
That's Kjartan!

00:47:21.240 --> 00:47:25.320
Remember him?

00:47:26.000 --> 00:47:28.960
That must be Sven.

00:47:29.040 --> 00:47:30.840
This is wrong.

00:47:29.040 --> 00:47:30.840
We need to tell Ragnar.

00:47:30.920 --> 00:47:32.880
They are between us

00:47:30.920 --> 00:47:32.880
and the wall.

00:47:32.960 --> 00:47:36.360
Then we go up and around,

00:47:32.960 --> 00:47:36.360
we leave the horses and run.

00:47:42.760 --> 00:47:45.720
[whispering] In front of

00:47:42.760 --> 00:47:45.720
the door. That's it!

00:47:54.800 --> 00:47:57.200
[dog barking]

00:48:04.840 --> 00:48:07.560
Ragnar, smoke!

00:48:08.600 --> 00:48:09.640
Fire!

00:48:09.720 --> 00:48:10.960
Hoo-rah! Wake up!

00:48:11.040 --> 00:48:14.320
...wake up! Fire!

00:48:14.400 --> 00:48:16.600
[screaming]

00:48:21.440 --> 00:48:23.080
[Ragnar]

00:48:21.440 --> 00:48:23.080
Come on! come on!

00:48:23.160 --> 00:48:26.440
[man] This way. Ravn!

00:48:26.520 --> 00:48:29.000
Come. Come quickly.

00:48:29.080 --> 00:48:30.520
Come!

00:48:31.120 --> 00:48:32.360
[coughing]

00:48:32.440 --> 00:48:35.560
-The door is blocked!

00:48:32.440 --> 00:48:35.560
-So is this one!

00:48:38.760 --> 00:48:40.280
Be ready.

00:48:40.360 --> 00:48:42.280
[screaming]

00:48:42.360 --> 00:48:44.360
This one's open,

00:48:42.360 --> 00:48:44.360
this one's open!

00:48:44.440 --> 00:48:47.160
come on, follow me. This way.

00:48:47.920 --> 00:48:50.200
[screaming]

00:48:53.080 --> 00:48:55.240
[speaks indistinct]

00:48:59.640 --> 00:49:00.840
[man] Archers!

00:49:00.920 --> 00:49:03.160
Don't go up there, wait for me!

00:49:03.240 --> 00:49:04.840
Come. Come!

00:49:06.760 --> 00:49:08.600
Ragnar!

00:49:08.680 --> 00:49:10.840
Close the doors,

00:49:08.680 --> 00:49:10.840
we have Thyra,

00:49:10.920 --> 00:49:12.440
Let the rest burn.

00:49:23.120 --> 00:49:25.080
[grunts]

00:50:09.160 --> 00:50:13.000
Take her with you to Valhalla.

00:50:13.080 --> 00:50:15.720
-Yes.

00:50:13.080 --> 00:50:15.720
-I will meet you there.

00:50:30.240 --> 00:50:32.960
[yelling]

00:50:44.080 --> 00:50:46.520
[grunting]

00:50:57.120 --> 00:50:59.720
[screaming]

00:51:04.360 --> 00:51:06.720
Oh, no...

00:51:11.280 --> 00:51:13.320
Find the silver!

00:51:14.280 --> 00:51:15.800
Now!

00:51:24.000 --> 00:51:27.400
[men speaking indistinct]

00:51:27.480 --> 00:51:30.160
They're searching

00:51:27.480 --> 00:51:30.160
for Ragnar's wealth.

00:51:31.600 --> 00:51:33.000
They'll never find it.

00:51:33.080 --> 00:51:37.320
Search in the back!

00:51:33.080 --> 00:51:37.320
Come on, were leaving soon.

00:51:39.760 --> 00:51:44.840
You thought I'd let you

00:51:39.760 --> 00:51:44.840
marry someone else.

00:51:47.560 --> 00:51:54.280
But... do you know what I will

00:51:47.560 --> 00:51:54.280
do with this body...

00:51:54.680 --> 00:51:58.280
...this mouth?

00:52:02.840 --> 00:52:08.760
I will do all I have

00:52:02.840 --> 00:52:08.760
dreamt of... and more.

00:52:08.840 --> 00:52:11.800
And who will call a halt?

00:52:13.480 --> 00:52:17.360
Earl Ragnar the fearless,

00:52:13.480 --> 00:52:17.360
is gone.

00:52:17.440 --> 00:52:21.400
And with him, Uhtred,

00:52:21.480 --> 00:52:27.400
his Saxon pet;

00:52:21.480 --> 00:52:27.400
a pile of ashes.

00:52:34.880 --> 00:52:37.080
Anything.

00:52:45.840 --> 00:52:47.240
Get down!

00:52:47.320 --> 00:52:51.160
Look at that man, the Saxon.

00:52:47.320 --> 00:52:51.160
His name is Scallion.

00:52:51.240 --> 00:52:54.400
He works with my uncle.

00:52:51.240 --> 00:52:54.400
He'll tell him that I'm dead.

00:52:54.480 --> 00:52:57.800
-Let him do it.

00:52:54.480 --> 00:52:57.800
-I see him with Kjartan.

00:52:57.880 --> 00:52:59.400
[Kjartan] Burn it to the ground.

00:52:59.480 --> 00:53:01.160
[Brida] He and your uncle,

00:52:59.480 --> 00:53:01.160
maybe they're in it together?

00:53:01.240 --> 00:53:03.600
And what makes them believe they

00:53:01.240 --> 00:53:03.600
can do this without punishment?

00:53:03.680 --> 00:53:07.240
Shh! They will be punished,

00:53:03.680 --> 00:53:07.240
but not by you.

00:53:07.320 --> 00:53:13.280
Uhtred, listen to me, we serve Ragnar

00:53:07.320 --> 00:53:13.280
best alive, we tell the story.

00:53:13.360 --> 00:53:16.160
-I need to kill someone.

00:53:13.360 --> 00:53:16.160
-No.

00:53:16.240 --> 00:53:17.960
And I choose him.

00:53:20.440 --> 00:53:22.000
Uhtred, no!

00:53:22.840 --> 00:53:24.120
Come on!

00:53:25.200 --> 00:53:28.600
[men yelling indistinct]

00:53:30.080 --> 00:53:31.720
[sighs]

00:53:34.880 --> 00:53:37.320
[laughing]

00:53:40.240 --> 00:53:43.240
[Kjartan] The main thing is to

00:53:40.240 --> 00:53:43.240
keep the horses together, yeah.

00:53:44.240 --> 00:53:47.480
Don't leave any weapons behind.

00:53:47.560 --> 00:53:50.120
Move those over

00:53:47.560 --> 00:53:50.120
and we'll look in the back.

00:53:50.200 --> 00:53:53.640
Don't leave anything in there

00:53:50.200 --> 00:53:53.640
just bring it all out.

00:54:03.600 --> 00:54:06.160
[pants]

00:54:19.680 --> 00:54:22.200
-Yeah, come on.

00:54:19.680 --> 00:54:22.200
-[man] Over here!

00:54:22.680 --> 00:54:24.120
OK, come on.

00:54:24.600 --> 00:54:27.080
[grunts]

00:54:33.240 --> 00:54:36.160
You know who I am,

00:54:33.240 --> 00:54:36.160
it's me your looking for.

00:54:36.240 --> 00:54:37.400
[blade pierces skin]

00:54:36.240 --> 00:54:37.400
[grimaces]

00:54:37.480 --> 00:54:38.880
It's me your looking for.

00:54:38.960 --> 00:54:42.000
You remember me?

00:54:38.960 --> 00:54:42.000
You remember me?

00:54:42.080 --> 00:54:45.120
[groans]

00:54:46.480 --> 00:54:49.920
[panting]

00:55:03.600 --> 00:55:06.840
-There's no more! We are going.

00:55:03.600 --> 00:55:06.840
-Come on.

00:55:06.920 --> 00:55:09.520
Bring the horses.

00:55:26.600 --> 00:55:28.760
[sobs]

00:55:54.720 --> 00:55:56.400
[grunts]

00:56:16.520 --> 00:56:19.600
By right,

00:56:16.520 --> 00:56:19.600
it belongs to young Ragnar.

00:56:20.080 --> 00:56:21.320
Yes...

00:56:21.400 --> 00:56:24.120
But we spend what we need

00:56:21.400 --> 00:56:24.120
to spend; we stay alive.

00:56:24.200 --> 00:56:26.520
We tell the story and then what?

00:56:29.640 --> 00:56:32.320
We find a new Lord to serve.

00:56:37.320 --> 00:56:41.360
I will not stand by and have

00:56:37.320 --> 00:56:41.360
everything that is mine taken from me.

00:56:43.320 --> 00:56:45.440
I'm going back....

00:56:45.640 --> 00:56:47.400
Where?

00:56:49.040 --> 00:56:51.240
To the beginning.

00:57:37.760 --> 00:57:40.720
[horn blows]

00:57:53.040 --> 00:57:55.080
-Is it Scallion?

00:57:53.040 --> 00:57:55.080
-No, my Lord.

00:57:55.160 --> 00:57:58.800
-He looks like a Dane.

00:57:55.160 --> 00:57:58.800
-Could be one of Kjartan's men.

00:58:21.320 --> 00:58:25.440
I am Uhtred of Bebbanburg,

00:58:21.320 --> 00:58:25.440
and I shall take what is mine!

00:58:26.840 --> 00:58:29.240
Bebbanburg is mine!

00:58:30.480 --> 00:58:31.920
Horses!